AnySoundIsolator

This product includes software adapted from Inworld Voice Isolator
(https://github.com/inworld-ai/voice-isolator,
commit c73b3fab81a870410cbac50d2f05f25edc4d10aa),
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0):

    Inworld Voice Isolator
    Copyright 2026 Inworld AI

The adapted files are in Sources/AnySoundIsolator, and they are compiled
only with the MLX package trait:

- Internal/Inworld/InworldSelectiveScan.swift adapts the Metal kernel
  _METAL_SOURCE in src/inworld/voice_isolation/scan.py.
- Internal/Inworld/InworldNetwork.swift, InworldSpectralTransform.swift, and
  InworldConfiguration.swift port the network, its transforms, and its
  configuration from src/inworld/voice_isolation/model.py.
- Internal/Inworld/InworldWindowAssembler.swift ports the window placement
  of VoiceIsolatorNetwork.enhance in src/inworld/voice_isolation/model.py.
- Internal/Inworld/InworldAssetStore.swift copies the repository, revision,
  file name, size, and SHA-256 digest of voice-isolator-v1 from
  src/inworld/voice_isolation/registry.py.

Changes from the original: the code is rewritten in Swift for MLX; the Metal
kernel reads its sizes from the shapes of its inputs, always applies the gate,
and carries no state between calls; the window placement works on a stream
whose length is not known in advance; and only the offline model is ported.
Each adapted file starts with a notice that states its source and its changes.

The model weights are not part of this repository. The code downloads them
from https://huggingface.co/inworld/voice-isolator when an application asks
for them. Inworld's NOTICE says this about the weights:

    The model weights were trained on Inworld's first-party data, including
    data purchased from vendors under private terms, and on these third-party
    datasets:

    - VocalSet — CC BY 4.0, https://zenodo.org/records/1442513
    - IndicVoices-R — CC BY 4.0,
      https://huggingface.co/datasets/ai4bharat/indicvoices_r
    - VCTK — ODC-By 1.0, https://datashare.ed.ac.uk/handle/10283/2119

The test fixtures that scripts/fetch-fixtures.sh downloads are not part of
this repository. They include a modified LibriSpeech recording under
CC BY 4.0; see tests/fixtures/README.md in Inworld's repository.
